b0F (1955). The low of <strong>35\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13.","t_rec":"Wheeling has nearly stopped setting record lows","p_rec":"If Wheeling's climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Wheeling has set <strong class=\"sig\">12 standing record lows</strong>, far fewer than the 78 that chance alone would give, and <strong>47 record highs</strong>, fewer than the 79 that chance alone would give. The 1930s hold the most record highs of any decade (86). Wheeling's all-time high is 106\u00b0F, on August 6, 1918.","t_chg":"Wheeling's nights got warmer. Its days didn't.","p_chg":"Across 116 complete years: Wheeling's average low has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.34\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.25 to +0.44), about +4.3\u00b0F since 1900. Wheeling's average high shows no clear change: +0.00\u00b0F per decade, a range (\u22120.11 to +0.12) that includes zero.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 11 of 12 months. Highs rose in 2 of 12 months; January fell.","t_rain":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Wheeling's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (\u22120.22 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 38.9 inches a year. The wettest year was 2018 (57.65 in); the driest, 1963 (27.34 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":true,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 3 daily record highs, 1 daily record low"}}